A||||17||86SE||Homemade anti-theft switch........||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||06-26-2000||07:03 PM||||Im pretty sure some of you have done this before, but im not sure how you did it.<P>To make an very very cheap anti-theft devise, all you have to do is make a hidden switch that cuts the power to the fuel pump.  Do i splice into any of the 2 wires that come to and from the fuel pump fuse in the fuse box?  Is this the easiest route?  There is already a very well hidden switch underneath the dash (you will only find it if you are lookin for it).<P>If I get this all hooked up, and plan to park the car overnight someware other than my garage, I park it, flip the switch, it will die, and not start until you flip the switch to turn the fuel pump back on, right? right....<P>But what I want to know is how easy is it to hot wire a Fiero??  People said they got to the parking lot and there Fiero was GONE!<P>Even if you had a key, you wont be able to start the car.............<P>Could save a Fiero.......or two||||reg||5
